/*
 * fallible-checkpoint.compact — first statement of a fallible section.
 *
 * Official reads (not invented APIs):
 *   kernel.checkpoint(): []
 *     https://docs.midnight.network/compact/reference/ledger-adt
 *     "Marks all execution up to this point as being a single atomic unit,
 *      allowing partial transaction failures to be split across it."
 *   Custom error 118 FallibleWithoutCheckpoint
 *     https://docs.midnight.network/nodes/error-codes
 *     "Fallible transcript missing initial checkpoint.
 *      Add kernel.checkpoint() at the start of fallible sections."
 *
 * Upstream: midnightntwrk/midnight-docs#1387
 * Kapa asked which Kernel operations exist (self, balance, blockTime, checkpoint).
 * checkpoint is a documented Kernel operation. It is not kernel.self().bytes.
 *
 * Language pin: Compact ~0.31.1 / language ~0.23.
 * Source only. Not compiled here. Not deployed.
